# ---------- Tome data artifacts ----------
# Generated by the knowledge pipeline and the app; all rebuildable, none belong in git.
tome.db
*.db
*.sqlite3
chroma_data/
chroma_db/
# Scryfall bulk downloads: ~24 MB gzipped per snapshot, and one is kept per
# snapshot date. `**/` matters — the importer caches under backend/data/scryfall,
# and a pattern containing a slash is otherwise anchored to the repo root.
**/data/scryfall/
*.bulk.json
*.jsonl.gz
# Hugging Face sentence-transformer weights, if cached in-repo.
.cache/
models/
# The metadata benchmark's run log and 300-card sample are the one exception
# to the *.db rule above and are tracked on purpose, not rebuilt blind: the
# sample is small, human-reviewed, and meant to be argued with in a diff
# (`knowledge_pipeline/benchmark/sample.py`), and the run log is the actual
# measured evidence a benchmark conclusion rests on -- losing it to a
# gitignore rule would hide the evidence, not just discard a rebuildable
# cache. `sample.json` needs no exception here: nothing above ignores *.json.
!backend/knowledge_pipeline/benchmark/benchmark.db
# The store has no migration path by design, so a schema bump retires the file
# rather than upgrading it. The retired one is kept for the same reason the
# live one is tracked -- it holds the only copy of what S-001 to S-003
# measured, and re-deriving it is impossible now that the harness makes
# production's two calls instead of one. Reading it needs the version-2 code
# from git history; what those sessions *established* is written into
# docs/benchmarking-and-testing.md and docs/lessons-learned.md.
!backend/knowledge_pipeline/benchmark/benchmark-v2-sessions-001-003.db
# The rendered report is not evidence, it is a view of it: 1.2 MB of HTML
# regenerable from benchmark.db by `benchmark report --html`. Tracking the
# store and not its rendering is the whole point of the exception above.
backend/knowledge_pipeline/benchmark/benchmark-report.html
# The archived contended-VRAM run, kept locally while diagnosing the 14B's
# memory spill. Not evidence for a conclusion -- delete it when done.
backend/knowledge_pipeline/benchmark/benchmark-contended.db

# ---------- Claude Code ----------
# settings.json is shared; settings.local.json is per-machine.
.claude/settings.local.json
